# lowered from the probe call.json by the fixture lowering (private tooling)
# The lane runs `ds-formal-tests --fixture` on this and diffs against
# call.expected (scripts/formal/check_idris.py). The call surface on Rete/NetworkCall.idr's engine. Kind
# 0 Reply is svc.read's response schema and kind 3 CallError the built-in the
# lowering synthesizes (LCRS.4.2.1), the two `answer` records with `corr` at
# payload slot 0; kind 1 Trig is logical on the key `k` and kind 2 Probe
# explicit. Rule 0 `r` has one call site at position 0 (no emit before it):
# svc.read, window 10 units, response kind 0, the key `slot 0 key 0`
# (Trig's `k`, LCRS.8.2), one argument `n: t.k`, the correlation "c1"
# (token 0). The `string` records give every token its text, the sweeps
# comparing correlations as texts (the lowering's THE STRING TABLE): "c1",
# the CallError's code and its message. Rule 1 `seen` logs the Reply's `v`.
# The time map's unit is 1 s:
# the TTLs 3600 and 300, the window 10, the ticks 5 and 11. Pump 1 issues
# the call (`call 0 0 svc.read s:0 i:1`) with nothing to sweep; the reply
# v1 arrives and pump 2 logs it; at 5 the Trig changes, `r` fires and the
# site's gate refuses the call -- no `call` line, the reply stays; at 11
# the gate admits and the call sweeps the reply before it is issued
# (LCRS.6.2.1); a reply v2 enters, a CallError sweeps it (LCRS.6.2.4), a
# reply v3 sweeps the error, and pump 5 logs v3.
schema 0 explicit Reply
schema 1 entity Trig
schema 2 explicit Probe
schema 3 explicit CallError
ttl 0 3600
ttl 3 300
alpha 0 0
alpha 1 1
alpha 2 2
alpha 3 3
answer 0 response pay 0
answer 3 error pay 0
string 0 2 99 49
string 1 17 116 114 97 110 115 112 111 114 116 46 116 105 109 101 111 117 116
string 2 8 110 111 32 114 111 117 116 101
rule 0 r
pattern 0 1 0
callsite 0 0 0 svc.read 10 0 1 slot 0 key 0 1 slot 0 key 0 lit s:0
rule 1 seen
pattern 1 2 0
pattern 1 0 0
log 1 0 1 slot 1 pay 1
step assert _0 1 1000000000000000000018 1000000000000000000002
step pump
step assert _1 0 1 1000000000000000000003000000000000000000018
step assert _2 2 1 1000000000000000000018
step pump
step tick 5
step assert _3 1 1000000000000000000018 1000000000000000000018
step pump
step tick 11
